## Glossary

| Term | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Packet | A piece of data that carries the address of where it is coming from and where it is going |
| Protocol | A set of rules that tells how data should be sent and received |
| Port | A number that uniquely identifies a service or an application on a device |
| Payload | The actual data being sent |
| Handshake | A process that prepares the client and server before any meaningful data is sent |

## Conclusion
This task showed me how much information can be read from network traffic. Using filters made it easy to isolate HTTP, DNS and TCP packets, and packet 212 showed how a login sent over HTTP exposes the username and password. It also showed why websites should use HTTPS.

